(3216763, 448776, 67258, '<td valign="top">A nice looking dog, but this photo doesn''t have that added ''thing'' that makes me want to look at it again.  The exposure is fine, but I think there are a number of things you could have done to inprove the photo: <br/><b>-</b> try experimenting with  different angles and perspectives, perhaps lying down on the floor with the dog, or if you want to take one from above, coming in much closer - this would help to avoid the snapshot look.<br/><b>- </b>make sure your sharpest point of focus is the dog''s eyes; here it appears to be further back, towards the shoulder.<br/><b>-</b>minor point,perhaps, but from the perspective of a ''non-doggy'' person, the exposed ears look rather unsettling - you may want to think about ensuring they are flipped forward.</td>', 'A nice looking dog, but this photo doesn''t have that added ''thing'' that makes me want to look at it again.  The exposure is fine, but I think there are a number of things you could have done to inprove the photo: - try experimenting with  different angles and perspectives, perhaps lying down on the floor with the dog, or if you want to take one from above, coming in much closer - this would help to avoid the snapshot look.- make sure your sharpest point of focus is the dog''s eyes; here it appears to be further back, towards the shoulder.-minor point,perhaps, but from the perspective of a ''non-doggy'' person, the exposed ears look rather unsettling - you may want to think about ensuring they are flipped forward.', '2007-01-12 04:52:41.000000', NULL, 1),
