(3218726, 451876, 6804, '<td valign="top">This is one of the best applications Ive seen for the pushed HDR/dragonized looking  processing.   In general Im not a big fan of the look.  Mostly because the photos Ive seen it used on would have looked better or more natural, without it.   I have seen this techniques done well here on DPC where the HDR adjustments were barely detectable and not pushed to the cartoon stage on landscapes and such.  I have seen the dragon filter used only a few times where I have actually liked the effect.  You have managed to successfully pair the pushed  HDR/dragon filter look (for lack of a better word) up with an animated expression.  Top-notch work in every way and to date this is my favorite animated looking processing here at DPC.  High marks from me.  Good luck in the challenge</td>', 'This is one of the best applications Ive seen for the pushed HDR/dragonized looking  processing.   In general Im not a big fan of the look.  Mostly because the photos Ive seen it used on would have looked better or more natural, without it.   I have seen this techniques done well here on DPC where the HDR adjustments were barely detectable and not pushed to the cartoon stage on landscapes and such.  I have seen the dragon filter used only a few times where I have actually liked the effect.  You have managed to successfully pair the pushed  HDR/dragon filter look (for lack of a better word) up with an animated expression.  Top-notch work in every way and to date this is my favorite animated looking processing here at DPC.  High marks from me.  Good luck in the challenge', '2007-01-12 11:31:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3218727, 448822, 27087, '<td valign="top">Great B&amp;W portrait</td>', 'Great B&W portrait', '2007-01-12 11:31:28.000000', NULL, 1),
