(3239148, 451842, 28710, '<td valign="top">I bet everyone and their dog is pointing this out, but you appear to have two spots of sensor dust.<br/> <br/>Put you lens in front of a smooth white paper, throw it in manual focus and make sure it is out of focus, then take a picture. You can use contrast adjustments to see the spots more clearly.<br/> <br/>Good to check every couple of weeks or more, depending on conditions.<br/> <br/>The photo would be a good candidate for a ''complexity'' challenge. In general, I find the pic a bit too busy. Also, the secondary/primary subject of the distant boat is centered which feels somewhat uncomfortable here.</td>', 'I bet everyone and their dog is pointing this out, but you appear to have two spots of sensor dust. Put you lens in front of a smooth white paper, throw it in manual focus and make sure it is out of focus, then take a picture. You can use contrast adjustments to see the spots more clearly. Good to check every couple of weeks or more, depending on conditions. The photo would be a good candidate for a ''complexity'' challenge. In general, I find the pic a bit too busy. Also, the secondary/primary subject of the distant boat is centered which feels somewhat uncomfortable here.', '2007-01-16 07:41:25.000000', NULL, 1),
