(3254482, 449035, 48560, '<td valign="top">i enjoy looking at travel photos - of buildings and places which i dont get to see often, or at all. and this is one of them. however, i''d like to honestly point out that there are 3 things on this image that distracts me:<br/>1. the halo around the 2 person in front. they dont appear to be main subjects of this composition (even if they are, they lack enough details). so the halo is more distraction than anything. <br/>2. horizon appears tilted - i haven''t gone and measured if it really is, but it appeared to be. it may have been caused by the perspective of the building itself, but i''d leave you with that.<br/>in a nutshell, i liked this photo, or i wouldn''t have bothered writing such a wrong comment. cheers!<br/>3. the border of this image - it''s minor issue, but i just thought i''d point it but and be honest about what i think (sorry)</td>', 'i enjoy looking at travel photos - of buildings and places which i dont get to see often, or at all. and this is one of them. however, i''d like to honestly point out that there are 3 things on this image that distracts me:1. the halo around the 2 person in front. they dont appear to be main subjects of this composition (even if they are, they lack enough details). so the halo is more distraction than anything. 2. horizon appears tilted - i haven''t gone and measured if it really is, but it appeared to be. it may have been caused by the perspective of the building itself, but i''d leave you with that.in a nutshell, i liked this photo, or i wouldn''t have bothered writing such a wrong comment. cheers!3. the border of this image - it''s minor issue, but i just thought i''d point it but and be honest about what i think (sorry)', '2007-01-19 03:00:07.000000', NULL, 1),
