(3284459, 451727, 60862, '<td valign="top">Oops.  My DQ was for an incorrectly set date, too.  Take solace in the fact that you''ll probably get a lot more views than if you''d been in the middle of the pack. :)<br/> <br/>Anyway, it''s a beautiful shot, and one that, despite the DQ, should help you remember the joy of standing in that spot.  I''m in the camp that likes how it looks like it''s on canvas.</td>', 'Oops.  My DQ was for an incorrectly set date, too.  Take solace in the fact that you''ll probably get a lot more views than if you''d been in the middle of the pack. :) Anyway, it''s a beautiful shot, and one that, despite the DQ, should help you remember the joy of standing in that spot.  I''m in the camp that likes how it looks like it''s on canvas.', '2007-01-26 01:54:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3284468, 448895, 63972, '<td valign="top">Wow, I was not aware that so many people on dpc have a serious allergy to selective saturation.  Well, it is good to know :-)))<br/> <br/>Nice catch about the halo-ing around the wings issue.  I must admit, I was lazy about the selection.  The color on the background was cyan-blue dominated, I did not bother doing any selection.  Well the halo is because of that ;-)<br/> <br/>As for the blown highlights, I agree. Again because of laziness...  I edited this version for printing and did not bother to edit it again for screen.<br/> <br/>Well, thanks for the comments, I appreciate them...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-27 16:54:34.</i></td>', 'Wow, I was not aware that so many people on dpc have a serious allergy to selective saturation.  Well, it is good to know :-))) Nice catch about the halo-ing around the wings issue.  I must admit, I was lazy about the selection.  The color on the background was cyan-blue dominated, I did not bother doing any selection.  Well the halo is because of that ;-) As for the blown highlights, I agree. Again because of laziness...  I edited this version for printing and did not bother to edit it again for screen. Well, thanks for the comments, I appreciate them...', '2007-01-26 01:55:53.000000', '2007-01-27 16:54:34.000000', 0),
