(3284724, 448864, 19708, '<td valign="top">Your statement: <i>"but I can honestly say it''s the best photo I''ve taken in 2006, if not EVER."</i> is so right on the money.<br/> <br/>I was very disappointed to see where this placed overall, but it''s kind of ironic isn''t it, that the more one of our own photographs moves us, the further down the scale they rank. I think it says something about what moves us deep inside for whatever reason, quite often in a different wavelength than the average crowd.<br/>It''s a far better thing to march to one''s own beat than to fall into the hum-drum kettle in life.</td>', 'Your statement: "but I can honestly say it''s the best photo I''ve taken in 2006, if not EVER." is so right on the money. I was very disappointed to see where this placed overall, but it''s kind of ironic isn''t it, that the more one of our own photographs moves us, the further down the scale they rank. I think it says something about what moves us deep inside for whatever reason, quite often in a different wavelength than the average crowd.It''s a far better thing to march to one''s own beat than to fall into the hum-drum kettle in life.', '2007-01-26 02:43:07.000000', NULL, 0),
