(3286060, 451444, 15497, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by whiterook:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Larus:</b></div><hr/><i> Well looks like there are about 9 people here on DPC that don´t like you Manny (the 1,2 &amp; 3 scores) but the rest thankfully are a bit more mature :)<br/> <br/>Congrat´s dude!  Don´t like this as much as your texture shot but that one was just friggin awesome, this is too of course and would have voted it an 8. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> That is not true  LARUS.  We don''t like the picture!!!!<br/>The picture is to dark crop is to much. Is this a Blue ribbon I will stick with Brown ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>whiterook, if you have a very dark calibration on your CRT/LCD, that might be true. But trust me when I say this is truly a masterpiece, and it''s perfectly exposed. You may wanna checkout a <a href="//www.colorvision.com/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Spyder</a>, to automatically calibrate your monitor. <br/> <br/>On my monitor your entries seem very overexposed, so I''m guessing it''s a calibration problem. <br/> <br/>Manny, A-W-E-S-O-M-E! Congrats with your blue!<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by whiterook: Originally posted by Larus: Well looks like there are about 9 people here on DPC that don´t like you Manny (the 1,2 & 3 scores) but the rest thankfully are a bit more mature :) Congrat´s dude!  Don´t like this as much as your texture shot but that one was just friggin awesome, this is too of course and would have voted it an 8.   That is not true  LARUS.  We don''t like the picture!!!!The picture is to dark crop is to much. Is this a Blue ribbon I will stick with Brown ribbon!   whiterook, if you have a very dark calibration on your CRT/LCD, that might be true. But trust me when I say this is truly a masterpiece, and it''s perfectly exposed. You may wanna checkout a Spyder, to automatically calibrate your monitor.  On my monitor your entries seem very overexposed, so I''m guessing it''s a calibration problem.  Manny, A-W-E-S-O-M-E! Congrats with your blue!', '2007-01-26 09:51:11.000000', NULL, 0),
