(3286092, 449036, 66384, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skiprow:</b></div><hr/><i> that''s a moment.  too bad you were so tight you could protect your horizon from the tilt-police ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I am usually among those referred to as the "tilt police", because a crooked horizon makes me uncomfortable. But in this shot, there is so much  wonderful action in the foreground, and the subject is so dramatic, I don''t mind the horizon at all.<br/> <br/>Great capture, I''m afraid to ask what happened next.</td>', 'Originally posted by skiprow: that''s a moment.  too bad you were so tight you could protect your horizon from the tilt-police ;-)  I am usually among those referred to as the "tilt police", because a crooked horizon makes me uncomfortable. But in this shot, there is so much  wonderful action in the foreground, and the subject is so dramatic, I don''t mind the horizon at all. Great capture, I''m afraid to ask what happened next.', '2007-01-26 09:59:21.000000', NULL, 0),
