(3287257, 451829, 5112, '<td valign="top">Hey, Neil, EXCELLENT!  Many congratulations to one of my most favourite photogs at DPC.  My daughter, Ximena, tells me she just loves this one.</td>', 'Hey, Neil, EXCELLENT!  Many congratulations to one of my most favourite photogs at DPC.  My daughter, Ximena, tells me she just loves this one.', '2007-01-26 14:14:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3287260, 451948, 66597, '<td valign="top">I really like this. I knew it would be too out there for DPC voters, but even as I voted, gave you a mental congrats for guts to enter it. I have this insane urge to play around with this photo, as I''d love to see it without the vertical red streaks directly to left of silo...anyway, cool stuff, keep on shooting!</td>', 'I really like this. I knew it would be too out there for DPC voters, but even as I voted, gave you a mental congrats for guts to enter it. I have this insane urge to play around with this photo, as I''d love to see it without the vertical red streaks directly to left of silo...anyway, cool stuff, keep on shooting!', '2007-01-26 14:16:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3287262, 451828, 66384, '<td valign="top">The fence in the background is a dead giveaway that this is a zoo or aviary shot. It doesn''t make the bird any less beautiful, but it does diminish the value of the image. As long as you were dealing with a captive bird, I think it would have been good to wait until the bird was leaning a little more toward you. Also if possible, get in a position where the branch is on a more interesting angle, possibly with a little background beneath it. If the branch is a horizontal perch you might try tilting the camera.<br/> <br/>Having said all that, I want you to know that I think the focus is good, the colors are lovely, and the Lory is adorable. I think you did a good job of capturing the sheen of the feathers without blowing out the highlights (hard to do). I hope you can go back and get lots more shots of this good subject.</td>', 'The fence in the background is a dead giveaway that this is a zoo or aviary shot. It doesn''t make the bird any less beautiful, but it does diminish the value of the image. As long as you were dealing with a captive bird, I think it would have been good to wait until the bird was leaning a little more toward you. Also if possible, get in a position where the branch is on a more interesting angle, possibly with a little background beneath it. If the branch is a horizontal perch you might try tilting the camera. Having said all that, I want you to know that I think the focus is good, the colors are lovely, and the Lory is adorable. I think you did a good job of capturing the sheen of the feathers without blowing out the highlights (hard to do). I hope you can go back and get lots more shots of this good subject.', '2007-01-26 14:16:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3287297, 448864, 6388, '<td valign="top">Criminal Placement.  Concur that this is a gem, and deserved MUCH better</td>', 'Criminal Placement.  Concur that this is a gem, and deserved MUCH better', '2007-01-26 14:25:23.000000', NULL, 0),
