(3288056, 450814, 42013, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fatLouie:</b></div><hr/><i> Good, but too soft! It looks as if you ran it over with a steamroller, flattening all the detail and reality of the photo<br/>But that could always be the ''wonderful'' 18-55 at work ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree with you... It was really soft and I couldn''t come up with a great way to improve the sharpness so i just went with the ''soft'' look. ;) It was before sunrise so the light was naturally soft, but...</td>', 'Originally posted by fatLouie: Good, but too soft! It looks as if you ran it over with a steamroller, flattening all the detail and reality of the photoBut that could always be the ''wonderful'' 18-55 at work ;)   I agree with you... It was really soft and I couldn''t come up with a great way to improve the sharpness so i just went with the ''soft'' look. ;) It was before sunrise so the light was naturally soft, but...', '2007-01-26 17:05:23.000000', NULL, 0),
