(3288912, 448504, 57791, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the comments!! Now that I look again at the photo I do see the skew or the trees leaning. I know that the camera was purfectly level as I used the leveling buble on the tripod. Thus I''m not sure why the photo looks skewed( any thoughts???) As usual I over sat every photo but in this particular case I oversat the photo because I had it printed on canvas which desats the photo some.<br/> <br/>I would have to disagree with the sky comments... looking at the photo closely it is exactly as I remember it. Perhaps its a bit off looking because the photo was taken at about 8000 feet????<br/> <br/>Again thank you all for the comments!! PLEASE continue offering thoughts.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thank you for the comments!! Now that I look again at the photo I do see the skew or the trees leaning. I know that the camera was purfectly level as I used the leveling buble on the tripod. Thus I''m not sure why the photo looks skewed( any thoughts???) As usual I over sat every photo but in this particular case I oversat the photo because I had it printed on canvas which desats the photo some. I would have to disagree with the sky comments... looking at the photo closely it is exactly as I remember it. Perhaps its a bit off looking because the photo was taken at about 8000 feet???? Again thank you all for the comments!! PLEASE continue offering thoughts. ', '2007-01-26 21:32:28.000000', NULL, 0),
