(3289435, 449878, 19708, '<td valign="top">Thank You for sharing such a joy to behold.<br/>After a few years on this site, the menu changes little with only variations in the recipes used, but this shot stands out all on it own, filled with a magical enchantment of sorts, and a color palette that truly does it justice.<br/>Congrats on your 21st place in this humongous challenge Steve.</td>', 'Thank You for sharing such a joy to behold.After a few years on this site, the menu changes little with only variations in the recipes used, but this shot stands out all on it own, filled with a magical enchantment of sorts, and a color palette that truly does it justice.Congrats on your 21st place in this humongous challenge Steve.', '2007-01-27 00:11:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3289440, 449446, 48890, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by agenkin:</b></div><hr/><i> I remember seeing another shot of the same scene, but could not find it right now.  I think that I like this variant better; will have to come again after the challenge is finished. 9 </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Aha, so I saw this exact shot, so long for my memory telling me that the gull was in a different position the previous time I saw this scene.  I didn''t remember it was buy you, so I searched in the wrong places when I voted.<br/> <br/>You know, without the gull''s shadow, this photograph would be falling apart, cut in two halves by the embankment''s edge.  But the shadow is there, and this is a pretty strong image.  I would lose the title, though: it''s hard to tell that the guy is reading a newspaper, and it doesn''t really matter, at least in my perception.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-27 00:13:36.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by agenkin: I remember seeing another shot of the same scene, but could not find it right now.  I think that I like this variant better; will have to come again after the challenge is finished. 9  Aha, so I saw this exact shot, so long for my memory telling me that the gull was in a different position the previous time I saw this scene.  I didn''t remember it was buy you, so I searched in the wrong places when I voted. You know, without the gull''s shadow, this photograph would be falling apart, cut in two halves by the embankment''s edge.  But the shadow is there, and this is a pretty strong image.  I would lose the title, though: it''s hard to tell that the guy is reading a newspaper, and it doesn''t really matter, at least in my perception.', '2007-01-27 00:12:15.000000', '2007-01-27 00:13:36.000000', 0),
