(3295393, 449225, 45187, '<td valign="top">Very very very cool</td>', 'Very very very cool', '2007-01-28 22:44:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295463, 451190, 62318, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful photo. I really like the choice of colors and framing done here. Not sure if the color tint was added in post or natural but it really give it a good vibe. The composition is near perfect, though I think the sun coming off the column seems a bit harsh. Also, I think it is a tad over-sharpened for this resolution as the individual and the top column shows definite signs of jaggedness. Still, a terrific photo!<br/> <br/>P.S. Much better than anything I was able to grab out of Venice.</td>', 'This is a wonderful photo. I really like the choice of colors and framing done here. Not sure if the color tint was added in post or natural but it really give it a good vibe. The composition is near perfect, though I think the sun coming off the column seems a bit harsh. Also, I think it is a tad over-sharpened for this resolution as the individual and the top column shows definite signs of jaggedness. Still, a terrific photo! P.S. Much better than anything I was able to grab out of Venice.', '2007-01-28 23:06:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295467, 448858, 62318, '<td valign="top">The exposure is spot on! As well a very nicely framed composition. I love the expression on the animal. I always think it is a plus when the animal can be humanized. For some reason the background seems a little wonky, a bit to grainy in some areas and a bit blurry in others, but just a minor nitpick. An excellent photograph!</td>', 'The exposure is spot on! As well a very nicely framed composition. I love the expression on the animal. I always think it is a plus when the animal can be humanized. For some reason the background seems a little wonky, a bit to grainy in some areas and a bit blurry in others, but just a minor nitpick. An excellent photograph!', '2007-01-28 23:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295476, 449578, 62318, '<td valign="top">I love how there are just 3 main colors, black, red and green and the pop of yellow that comes through. Also how the colors repeat throughout the frame is a working plus. Very rich colors. I might have cropped just a bit off the bottom myself to remove the other yellow spots, but that is just a minor nitpick. Wonderful photo and glad it did well for you!</td>', 'I love how there are just 3 main colors, black, red and green and the pop of yellow that comes through. Also how the colors repeat throughout the frame is a working plus. Very rich colors. I might have cropped just a bit off the bottom myself to remove the other yellow spots, but that is just a minor nitpick. Wonderful photo and glad it did well for you!', '2007-01-28 23:12:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295487, 447960, 62318, '<td valign="top">A beautiful photo. The repeating patterns and colors are stellar. The lighting is surperb and focus great. I like the use of depth here, but making the way you implemented is almost begging for the central focus to be a "different" flower or color (or maybe if all the other flowers were pure red). This is purely a subjective thing. Beyond this though, nearly everything is perfect. A terrific capture.</td>', 'A beautiful photo. The repeating patterns and colors are stellar. The lighting is surperb and focus great. I like the use of depth here, but making the way you implemented is almost begging for the central focus to be a "different" flower or color (or maybe if all the other flowers were pure red). This is purely a subjective thing. Beyond this though, nearly everything is perfect. A terrific capture.', '2007-01-28 23:16:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295498, 451813, 62318, '<td valign="top">I can see why you like this one. The side lighting is very original. The textures is makes in the trees and the range from white to black is very unique. I''d be almost tempted to make this a vertical panaromic format since I think some of the left side isn''t helping the photo. This is the type of photo that gives me alot of ideas for my own shots. I like it!</td>', 'I can see why you like this one. The side lighting is very original. The textures is makes in the trees and the range from white to black is very unique. I''d be almost tempted to make this a vertical panaromic format since I think some of the left side isn''t helping the photo. This is the type of photo that gives me alot of ideas for my own shots. I like it!', '2007-01-28 23:21:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295515, 450772, 62318, '<td valign="top">A terrific silhoutte, man on top of the world capture. I like the gently slope of the mountain which I think adds a tremendous amount and helps move your eye left to right. The person walking also helps with the same eye movement. The rounded clouds then moves you back the other way. Finally, the centered sun lining up with the bottom folks brings you up and down. As you can tell, eye movement is terrific here. A wonderful photograph.</td>', 'A terrific silhoutte, man on top of the world capture. I like the gently slope of the mountain which I think adds a tremendous amount and helps move your eye left to right. The person walking also helps with the same eye movement. The rounded clouds then moves you back the other way. Finally, the centered sun lining up with the bottom folks brings you up and down. As you can tell, eye movement is terrific here. A wonderful photograph.', '2007-01-28 23:25:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295533, 447517, 62318, '<td valign="top">Those clouds are very cool, similiar to the Aurora. The overall composition of this is terrific. A good showcase of near/middle/far or triangles (whatever you want to call it). It really helps with the eye movement. I like the detail here and the nice lighting in the background mountain. I love the pose of the hiker, though I don''t like how he is very dark. Fill light would have brought this to the next level or going the opposite pure silhoutte. Still a great capture.</td>', 'Those clouds are very cool, similiar to the Aurora. The overall composition of this is terrific. A good showcase of near/middle/far or triangles (whatever you want to call it). It really helps with the eye movement. I like the detail here and the nice lighting in the background mountain. I love the pose of the hiker, though I don''t like how he is very dark. Fill light would have brought this to the next level or going the opposite pure silhoutte. Still a great capture.', '2007-01-28 23:29:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295560, 447620, 62318, '<td valign="top">The detail on this photo is superb. Very few photos are this detailed, as this is a combination of spot on focus, great lighting and understanding of white balance. The complimentry colors work very well together. I''m not sure that I like the centered composition, but that is more personal taste. A terrific photo.</td>', 'The detail on this photo is superb. Very few photos are this detailed, as this is a combination of spot on focus, great lighting and understanding of white balance. The complimentry colors work very well together. I''m not sure that I like the centered composition, but that is more personal taste. A terrific photo.', '2007-01-28 23:34:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295573, 451780, 62318, '<td valign="top">You have managed to capture a very cute moment in time. Wonderful timing of the photo.I think the focus might be just a tad off, but nothing to get excited about. I would almost be tempted to convert this to B&amp;W since the green grass really since to contradict the monochromatic scene.I love the vertical lines you created in both the legs and trunk. A very nice capture.</td>', 'You have managed to capture a very cute moment in time. Wonderful timing of the photo.I think the focus might be just a tad off, but nothing to get excited about. I would almost be tempted to convert this to B&W since the green grass really since to contradict the monochromatic scene.I love the vertical lines you created in both the legs and trunk. A very nice capture.', '2007-01-28 23:37:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295581, 451844, 62318, '<td valign="top">A terrific "real world" type of photo. I like the B&amp;W treament here. The exposure is spot on. I like the multitude of lines you have managed to create here. I might have preferred the child on the bottom to be fully in the frame, but I love his pose. A very special type of photo.</td>', 'A terrific "real world" type of photo. I like the B&W treament here. The exposure is spot on. I like the multitude of lines you have managed to create here. I might have preferred the child on the bottom to be fully in the frame, but I love his pose. A very special type of photo.', '2007-01-28 23:38:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295593, 450290, 62318, '<td valign="top">Great ethereal feeling going on here. The lines of the fencing is terrific, and I like how you put them slightly off center as generally you see these types of shots straight on. The horizon is slightly leaning which is a slight niggle. It appears to have a very difficult shot exposure wise. Considering all things it is well done. I might try a grad ND filter for this type next time and try to brighten the few trees afterwards. Still, I really enjoyed this photo!</td>', 'Great ethereal feeling going on here. The lines of the fencing is terrific, and I like how you put them slightly off center as generally you see these types of shots straight on. The horizon is slightly leaning which is a slight niggle. It appears to have a very difficult shot exposure wise. Considering all things it is well done. I might try a grad ND filter for this type next time and try to brighten the few trees afterwards. Still, I really enjoyed this photo!', '2007-01-28 23:41:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295611, 449001, 62318, '<td valign="top">This is one of the best "bird on a wire" photos I have seen. What makes it is the two interactive birds which helps fill in the negative space so common in this type of photo. I also like the gradual background color transition, it really concides with the line nicely. I also like the fact of the one brown bird. It is the "different" things in this often photographed idea that make this one a winner. A terrific photo.</td>', 'This is one of the best "bird on a wire" photos I have seen. What makes it is the two interactive birds which helps fill in the negative space so common in this type of photo. I also like the gradual background color transition, it really concides with the line nicely. I also like the fact of the one brown bird. It is the "different" things in this often photographed idea that make this one a winner. A terrific photo.', '2007-01-28 23:44:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295626, 447785, 62318, '<td valign="top">The detail is incredible here. I love the unusual pose of the bee. I have never seen one quite like this.The colors pop really well. I think the only things hold it back are the busy background for this type of photo and maybe a slightly different angle. Still a terrific macro photo.</td>', 'The detail is incredible here. I love the unusual pose of the bee. I have never seen one quite like this.The colors pop really well. I think the only things hold it back are the busy background for this type of photo and maybe a slightly different angle. Still a terrific macro photo.', '2007-01-28 23:46:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295642, 447773, 62318, '<td valign="top">I love the mimiced pose and the general direction they are looking. The tail makes a wonderful line throughout the frame, though I would have liked to see the end of it. White balance seems a little off (too blue), and fixing that alone would make the colors really pop. Still a great capture of some very incredible animals.</td>', 'I love the mimiced pose and the general direction they are looking. The tail makes a wonderful line throughout the frame, though I would have liked to see the end of it. White balance seems a little off (too blue), and fixing that alone would make the colors really pop. Still a great capture of some very incredible animals.', '2007-01-28 23:48:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295656, 449830, 62318, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colors going on here. The lighting you captures is surperb. I love the lines you created with the grass it moves your eye throughout the frame but leads you to the upper right which circles distract a bit. Though I think that has more to do with the actual lens in this case, because I think the use of depth you were use was a good idea. Focus is great. A really nice capture.</td>', 'Beautiful colors going on here. The lighting you captures is surperb. I love the lines you created with the grass it moves your eye throughout the frame but leads you to the upper right which circles distract a bit. Though I think that has more to do with the actual lens in this case, because I think the use of depth you were use was a good idea. Focus is great. A really nice capture.', '2007-01-28 23:51:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295668, 451649, 62318, '<td valign="top">I terrific composition. I think there a just a few things I would challenge to make this a perfect picture. I might trim off a bit of the top, maybe 8x10 format. I like the colors here, though maybe a bit too much saturation was added to the orange channel. I do like the mood you are conveying here. It is one of those special photos though, and makes me wish I could visit Thailand again. A real winner in my eyes.</td>', 'I terrific composition. I think there a just a few things I would challenge to make this a perfect picture. I might trim off a bit of the top, maybe 8x10 format. I like the colors here, though maybe a bit too much saturation was added to the orange channel. I do like the mood you are conveying here. It is one of those special photos though, and makes me wish I could visit Thailand again. A real winner in my eyes.', '2007-01-28 23:54:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295714, 451878, 62318, '<td valign="top">A fun different type of landscape. Not sure if the curvature was intentional, but I think it adds a great dimension to the photo, almost like a reverse ocean scene. The varied colored tones add alot of interest and the brown pop works wonders. Not sure of the exposure, but the clouds seem a little soft, it might be due to a long exposure.</td>', 'A fun different type of landscape. Not sure if the curvature was intentional, but I think it adds a great dimension to the photo, almost like a reverse ocean scene. The varied colored tones add alot of interest and the brown pop works wonders. Not sure of the exposure, but the clouds seem a little soft, it might be due to a long exposure.', '2007-01-29 00:05:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295787, 451948, 62318, '<td valign="top">Uh Oh, pop art. Na, this is good stuff. It''s hard to wrap my brain around sometimes, but I like the ideas here. The accents of color, the boldness of yellow and the subdued green really work well. Compositional it is near perfect, sure there is the cut off cow, but I realize that is the intent. There is a difference between missing the composition because of "mistakes" and missing the composition because of "intent". I see alot of intent here. The only compostion "mistake" I see here is the flower covering the house.<br/> <br/>This is one of those photos that is more than just the exposure, lighting, composition. People who do not understand that I think are just missing out on the point. Photography doesn''t have to be all mechnical. You have a special photo here. It''s purposeful without being just a gimmick. A wonderful treat to see. Simply surreal.</td>', 'Uh Oh, pop art. Na, this is good stuff. It''s hard to wrap my brain around sometimes, but I like the ideas here. The accents of color, the boldness of yellow and the subdued green really work well. Compositional it is near perfect, sure there is the cut off cow, but I realize that is the intent. There is a difference between missing the composition because of "mistakes" and missing the composition because of "intent". I see alot of intent here. The only compostion "mistake" I see here is the flower covering the house. This is one of those photos that is more than just the exposure, lighting, composition. People who do not understand that I think are just missing out on the point. Photography doesn''t have to be all mechnical. You have a special photo here. It''s purposeful without being just a gimmick. A wonderful treat to see. Simply surreal.', '2007-01-29 00:14:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295816, 451828, 62318, '<td valign="top">Great sharpness and terrific colors. I like the overal composition. A very good understand of what makes a photo appealing. The fence is a little bit of a distraction, but not because of the design. I actually think the pattern helps here, but it is the fact that the view knows what the background entails. Still a wonderful capture.</td>', 'Great sharpness and terrific colors. I like the overal composition. A very good understand of what makes a photo appealing. The fence is a little bit of a distraction, but not because of the design. I actually think the pattern helps here, but it is the fact that the view knows what the background entails. Still a wonderful capture.', '2007-01-29 00:16:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295851, 448399, 62318, '<td valign="top">This is a terrific candid moment giving alot of context to the even occuring. Not sure if I like the direction of the color tint, but that is subjectional. I feel the same about the tilt. A tough shot to nail, but pretty good exposure wise. A fun candid shot.</td>', 'This is a terrific candid moment giving alot of context to the even occuring. Not sure if I like the direction of the color tint, but that is subjectional. I feel the same about the tilt. A tough shot to nail, but pretty good exposure wise. A fun candid shot.', '2007-01-29 00:19:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295870, 448416, 62318, '<td valign="top">A great beach scene here. The clouds and lines are terrific. I think it would help the composition a bit if you were able to see the curve in the bend and the horizon is slightly titled. I do love the waves and textures, and the eye movement in the photo is good. A great capture.</td>', 'A great beach scene here. The clouds and lines are terrific. I think it would help the composition a bit if you were able to see the curve in the bend and the horizon is slightly titled. I do love the waves and textures, and the eye movement in the photo is good. A great capture.', '2007-01-29 00:20:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295901, 449258, 62318, '<td valign="top">This is a photo all about context. It is quite funny, but seems to be missing the intergrity of the scene to actually make it work. The two seem a little non-chalant about the whole thing. Nevertheless I like the idea here. The location was a terrific choice. Colors are great. Focus is a bit soft, but the exposure is great, more especially consider the difficult lighting.</td>', 'This is a photo all about context. It is quite funny, but seems to be missing the intergrity of the scene to actually make it work. The two seem a little non-chalant about the whole thing. Nevertheless I like the idea here. The location was a terrific choice. Colors are great. Focus is a bit soft, but the exposure is great, more especially consider the difficult lighting.', '2007-01-29 00:23:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3295953, 447903, 62318, '<td valign="top">Great composition. I like the "crop" you did here? I''m guessing a crop because of the slight soft-focus. The colors are great. I actually like the context here, as you usually seem this types of shot with a blurred background. I would almost be tempted to lower the exposure a bit though to bring the yellow against the black a bit more. Still a great photograph.</td>', 'Great composition. I like the "crop" you did here? I''m guessing a crop because of the slight soft-focus. The colors are great. I actually like the context here, as you usually seem this types of shot with a blurred background. I would almost be tempted to lower the exposure a bit though to bring the yellow against the black a bit more. Still a great photograph.', '2007-01-29 00:28:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3296006, 451662, 62318, '<td valign="top">A classic image! Great lines, terrific light. The catch of red. The only thing is it is more or less a reproduction of a style. A very, very good reproduction but I think it takes a bit away from the image. I do like your take on the subject. Strictly on the merit on the technical side it is near perfect. A terrific shot.</td>', 'A classic image! Great lines, terrific light. The catch of red. The only thing is it is more or less a reproduction of a style. A very, very good reproduction but I think it takes a bit away from the image. I do like your take on the subject. Strictly on the merit on the technical side it is near perfect. A terrific shot.', '2007-01-29 00:32:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3296034, 451151, 62318, '<td valign="top">I like how you composed the shot, the way the child is looking into the frame gives at least a good use for the negative space. The focus seems a bit too soft, maybe just a bit more and it would be good. I have never been a fan of selective coloring unless there is a purpose. I guess your intent was to have the hat the subject of the image? Beyond that though, the pose is great and the lighting is wonderful. A nice image and very cute child.</td>', 'I like how you composed the shot, the way the child is looking into the frame gives at least a good use for the negative space. The focus seems a bit too soft, maybe just a bit more and it would be good. I have never been a fan of selective coloring unless there is a purpose. I guess your intent was to have the hat the subject of the image? Beyond that though, the pose is great and the lighting is wonderful. A nice image and very cute child.', '2007-01-29 00:35:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3296063, 449036, 62318, '<td valign="top">Terrific action shot. Not only is the action incredible (verticle jet ski), but the facial impression really sells the image. Color and exposure are right on. The only little things are the slight dip in horizon, the clipping of the jet ski on top, and maybe a bit too centered. This are just minor things to an otherwise excellent photograph!</td>', 'Terrific action shot. Not only is the action incredible (verticle jet ski), but the facial impression really sells the image. Color and exposure are right on. The only little things are the slight dip in horizon, the clipping of the jet ski on top, and maybe a bit too centered. This are just minor things to an otherwise excellent photograph!', '2007-01-29 00:38:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3296076, 451449, 62318, '<td valign="top">A terrific pose. Funny how he is giving you the bird. Colors are superb. The texture seems a little strange, maybe over-sharpened or missed focus? Still a great photo.</td>', 'A terrific pose. Funny how he is giving you the bird. Colors are superb. The texture seems a little strange, maybe over-sharpened or missed focus? Still a great photo.', '2007-01-29 00:40:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3296099, 447948, 62318, '<td valign="top">I love the idea of the black and white capture here. The lighting is terrific. Not sure of post though, as some might be a little overdone? Tree edges have a strange halo effect on the left side. Terrific framing of the head stones and good placement of the central subject. A great photo.</td>', 'I love the idea of the black and white capture here. The lighting is terrific. Not sure of post though, as some might be a little overdone? Tree edges have a strange halo effect on the left side. Terrific framing of the head stones and good placement of the central subject. A great photo.', '2007-01-29 00:43:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3296126, 447749, 62318, '<td valign="top">I really like the context of the action here. Great eye movement from left to right. There is something strange about the colors though, almost of the red dresses have too much brightness but not enough contrast? Curious if fill flash was used, or if the exposure was fixed in post? Still a great photo where the compostion and idea really shine through.</td>', 'I really like the context of the action here. Great eye movement from left to right. There is something strange about the colors though, almost of the red dresses have too much brightness but not enough contrast? Curious if fill flash was used, or if the exposure was fixed in post? Still a great photo where the compostion and idea really shine through.', '2007-01-29 00:45:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3296150, 451193, 51793, '<td valign="top">Good job buddy. Nicely captured and awesome effects.</td>', 'Good job buddy. Nicely captured and awesome effects.', '2007-01-29 00:49:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3296873, 448044, 36999, '<td valign="top">I was hoping this was yours.  It''s very nice for a competition photo.  Pretty amazingly clean background for a show grounds too.  -7 from me...  I know how hard it is to get one like this!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-29 03:41:29.</i></td>', 'I was hoping this was yours.  It''s very nice for a competition photo.  Pretty amazingly clean background for a show grounds too.  -7 from me...  I know how hard it is to get one like this!', '2007-01-29 03:39:18.000000', '2007-01-29 03:41:29.000000', 0),
(3297190, 448074, 48560, '<td valign="top">hi Robert - i was a little taken aback when i realize this was your "Best of 2006" submission. i guess you have your reasons, but i''m sure you have much more powerful images in your collection besides this submission. not saying this photo is bad, but it just isn''t your usual quality - if you get what i mean.</td>', 'hi Robert - i was a little taken aback when i realize this was your "Best of 2006" submission. i guess you have your reasons, but i''m sure you have much more powerful images in your collection besides this submission. not saying this photo is bad, but it just isn''t your usual quality - if you get what i mean.', '2007-01-29 05:20:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3297241, 449078, 5728, '<td valign="top">A pretty sucky placing for such a cool pic!</td>', 'A pretty sucky placing for such a cool pic!', '2007-01-29 05:39:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3297264, 451566, 22301, '<td valign="top">Hey congrats on the PB! (I was one of your nines)</td>', 'Hey congrats on the PB! (I was one of your nines)', '2007-01-29 05:54:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3297345, 451444, 66709, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by terje:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by whiterook:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Larus:</b></div><hr/><i> Well looks like there are about 9 people here on DPC that don´t like you Manny (the 1,2 &amp; 3 scores) but the rest thankfully are a bit more mature :)<br/> <br/>Congrat´s dude!  Don´t like this as much as your texture shot but that one was just friggin awesome, this is too of course and would have voted it an 8. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> That is not true  LARUS.  We don''t like the picture!!!!<br/>The picture is to dark crop is to much. Is this a Blue ribbon I will stick with Brown ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>whiterook, if you have a very dark calibration on your CRT/LCD, that might be true. But trust me when I say this is truly a masterpiece, and it''s perfectly exposed. You may wanna checkout a <a href="//www.colorvision.com/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Spyder</a>, to automatically calibrate your monitor. <br/> <br/>On my monitor your entries seem very overexposed, so I''m guessing it''s a calibration problem. <br/> <br/>Manny, A-W-E-S-O-M-E! Congrats with your blue! </i></td></tr></table> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/616/448525.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/616/448525.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/616/448525.jpg"/> <br/>This shot look great on my monitor terje</td>', 'Originally posted by terje: Originally posted by whiterook: Originally posted by Larus: Well looks like there are about 9 people here on DPC that don´t like you Manny (the 1,2 & 3 scores) but the rest thankfully are a bit more mature :) Congrat´s dude!  Don´t like this as much as your texture shot but that one was just friggin awesome, this is too of course and would have voted it an 8.   That is not true  LARUS.  We don''t like the picture!!!!The picture is to dark crop is to much. Is this a Blue ribbon I will stick with Brown ribbon!   whiterook, if you have a very dark calibration on your CRT/LCD, that might be true. But trust me when I say this is truly a masterpiece, and it''s perfectly exposed. You may wanna checkout a Spyder, to automatically calibrate your monitor.  On my monitor your entries seem very overexposed, so I''m guessing it''s a calibration problem.  Manny, A-W-E-S-O-M-E! Congrats with your blue!   This shot look great on my monitor terje', '2007-01-29 06:48:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3297472, 447625, 62812, '<td valign="top">Well done Rook!<br/>Absolute dross as usual.</td>', 'Well done Rook!Absolute dross as usual.', '2007-01-29 07:08:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3297478, 447625, 66709, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bood:</b></div><hr/><i> Well done Rook!<br/>Absolute dross as usual. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Bood</td>', 'Originally posted by bood: Well done Rook!Absolute dross as usual.   Thanks Bood', '2007-01-29 07:09:44.000000', NULL, 0),
