(3300592, 451444, 6388, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by whiterook:</b></div><hr/><i>  That is not true  LARUS.  We don''t like the picture!!!!<br/>The picture is to dark crop is to much. Is this a Blue ribbon I will stick with Brown ribbon! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>And you''ll likely get your wish, Whiterook.<br/> <br/>As for you, Manny...well - you already know what I think about the entire series with Rosalinda.  Pure Genius.  Ballsy and real...the way an A-Class artist should be ;)<br/> <br/>All the best, Pare...keep on bein'' you.<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'Originally posted by whiterook:  That is not true  LARUS.  We don''t like the picture!!!!The picture is to dark crop is to much. Is this a Blue ribbon I will stick with Brown ribbon!   And you''ll likely get your wish, Whiterook. As for you, Manny...well - you already know what I think about the entire series with Rosalinda.  Pure Genius.  Ballsy and real...the way an A-Class artist should be ;) All the best, Pare...keep on bein'' you. P', '2007-01-29 20:50:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300640, 447860, 64994, '<td valign="top">OMG!! what a cool shot!!! To echo pekesty''s comment, what an amazing B &amp; W conversion!! I am lucky to get that kind of range on film let alone digital!! Great job!!!<br/></td>', 'OMG!! what a cool shot!!! To echo pekesty''s comment, what an amazing B & W conversion!! I am lucky to get that kind of range on film let alone digital!! Great job!!!', '2007-01-29 20:58:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300807, 450781, 73031, '<td valign="top">Nice familia and a great shot. Not bad for 90 years old.</td>', 'Nice familia and a great shot. Not bad for 90 years old.', '2007-01-29 21:39:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300838, 451813, 66597, '<td valign="top">What a great job of capturing light and smoke together, filtering through trees. Gives a feeling of depth, and a lot of movement in those lines. Might like to see it in a simple frame to help it pop.</td>', 'What a great job of capturing light and smoke together, filtering through trees. Gives a feeling of depth, and a lot of movement in those lines. Might like to see it in a simple frame to help it pop.', '2007-01-29 21:48:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300850, 447620, 66597, '<td valign="top">Great colors, expression, and very sharp. This would be a very appealing easter card or diptych / triptych with other farm animals. (Not that it doesn''t stand well on its own - it does - just thinking aloud regarding commercial possibilities for this). The duckling looks so soft I want to pet her. You definitely appeal to emotion here.</td>', 'Great colors, expression, and very sharp. This would be a very appealing easter card or diptych / triptych with other farm animals. (Not that it doesn''t stand well on its own - it does - just thinking aloud regarding commercial possibilities for this). The duckling looks so soft I want to pet her. You definitely appeal to emotion here.', '2007-01-29 21:51:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300859, 448399, 66597, '<td valign="top">Chris,<br/>This is extra cool. I agree you should put the story in the comments section. I like the angle, graininess, and obvious candid expressions. So much more interesting than a staid portrait.</td>', 'Chris,This is extra cool. I agree you should put the story in the comments section. I like the angle, graininess, and obvious candid expressions. So much more interesting than a staid portrait.', '2007-01-29 21:53:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300884, 450290, 66597, '<td valign="top">I can understand why you are drawn to this shot as your fave for 2006. It has an ethereal, other-worldly feel that is captivating. Roads to some unknown destination, when captured thoughtfully, always make the viewer want to follow. A couple of minor points - I think the horizon, slightly tilted to right, probably cost you some points. I also think the water on the pavement could be toned down just a touch - but that is an artistic call, and just something I might try. Again, fabulous photo. Love it.</td>', 'I can understand why you are drawn to this shot as your fave for 2006. It has an ethereal, other-worldly feel that is captivating. Roads to some unknown destination, when captured thoughtfully, always make the viewer want to follow. A couple of minor points - I think the horizon, slightly tilted to right, probably cost you some points. I also think the water on the pavement could be toned down just a touch - but that is an artistic call, and just something I might try. Again, fabulous photo. Love it.', '2007-01-29 22:00:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300890, 451403, 9668, '<td valign="top">Awesome overlay, I really like this as well.</td>', 'Awesome overlay, I really like this as well.', '2007-01-29 22:01:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301284, 451829, 43437, '<td valign="top">Hey just getting to look around the best of and what do i find on the first page but this gem.  Truely beautiful neil, i think you chose right.</td>', 'Hey just getting to look around the best of and what do i find on the first page but this gem.  Truely beautiful neil, i think you chose right.', '2007-01-29 23:22:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301287, 447683, 43437, '<td valign="top">Sp stunning it takes my breath away!</td>', 'Sp stunning it takes my breath away!', '2007-01-29 23:24:15.000000', NULL, 0),
