(3655332, 447500, 34938, '<td valign="top">wow...stunning...congratulations on the NatGeo victory...we obviously can''t tell a good picture when we see one...103rd makes this way underrated</td>', 'wow...stunning...congratulations on the NatGeo victory...we obviously can''t tell a good picture when we see one...103rd makes this way underrated', '2007-05-16 10:57:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3659726, 448572, 28710, '<td valign="top">just had a thought. I wonder if you were to put a couple layers of sharpening on this quite strongly, but use the layers just to push the contrast at the edges of things... the result would be that you would get a bit more of a ''soft focus'' look (kind of looking like a layer of haze over an image that is sharp...)...<br/> <br/>just an idea. set the layer mode of one to darken and the other to lighten and play with radius and opacity on each layer... see what comes of it.</td>', 'just had a thought. I wonder if you were to put a couple layers of sharpening on this quite strongly, but use the layers just to push the contrast at the edges of things... the result would be that you would get a bit more of a ''soft focus'' look (kind of looking like a layer of haze over an image that is sharp...)... just an idea. set the layer mode of one to darken and the other to lighten and play with radius and opacity on each layer... see what comes of it.', '2007-05-17 11:10:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3659733, 450699, 28710, '<td valign="top">also try working the curves to remove that color cast... tutorial in tutorials section. blue channel is opposite to yellow, so push the blues and reds channel is opposite to Cyan... Play with the red/cyan after tweaking the blue/yellow.</td>', 'also try working the curves to remove that color cast... tutorial in tutorials section. blue channel is opposite to yellow, so push the blues and reds channel is opposite to Cyan... Play with the red/cyan after tweaking the blue/yellow.', '2007-05-17 11:12:51.000000', NULL, 0),
